  "term": "myoclonic epilepsy",
  "definition": "Myoclonic epilepsy is a varied group of epilepsy syndromes marked by myoclonic seizures, or by myoclonus occurring along with other kinds of seizures. These syndromes are commonly grouped by cause into familial, cryptogenic, and symptomatic forms.",
